{
  "openapi": "3.1.0",
  "info": {
    "title": "ASP.NET Core TodoApiDTO static-contract baseline",
    "version": "1.0.0",
    "x-basis": "Hand-written from the pinned, third-party source dotnet/AspNetCore.Docs @ 3d06f3ee297f0514cfade27232c1a266362f4f97, path aspnetcore/tutorials/first-web-api/samples/9.0/TodoApiDTO, independent of scanner output. This is the official Microsoft controller-based tutorial (not Minimal API): [ApiController] controllers on .NET 9 (net9.0, Nullable enabled) backed by EF Core InMemory. Contract decisions verified by reading the source and by running the app natively (dotnet SDK 10 with DOTNET_ROLL_FORWARD=LatestMajor): (1) [Route(\"api/[controller]\")] on TodoItemsController resolves to /api/TodoItems; WeatherForecastController uses [Route(\"[controller]\")] and its [HttpGet(Name = \"GetWeatherForecast\")] Name is the route NAME for URL generation, not a path template, so the route is /WeatherForecast (the extra /GetWeatherForecast segment returns 404). (2) The response projects TodoItem through ItemToDTO into TodoItemDTO { id:long, name:string?, isComplete:bool }; the entity's Secret property MUST NOT appear in any response (field-leak guard), enforced with x-audit-exact-properties. (3) System.Text.Json web defaults use camelCase and do not ignore nulls, so nullable keys (name, summary) are always present and stay required while carrying a null type. (4) Request DTO members are never implicitly required: value types (long id, bool isComplete) bind to default values when omitted and name is string?, so POST with an empty object returns 201; only the request body itself is required. (5) GET/PUT/DELETE return NotFound()/BadRequest()/NoContent() per branch; on ASP.NET Core 9 bodiless error StatusCodeResults are auto-filled with application/problem+json (RFC 7807) while 204 stays empty. (6) [ApiController] automatic model binding/validation returns 400 application/problem+json with an errors map, including a non-numeric {id} for the long route parameter. (7) POST returns CreatedAtAction(..., ItemToDTO) = 201 with the DTO; PUT success is 204; DELETE success is 204. (8) WeatherForecast exposes DateOnly Date as string format date and the read-only computed TemperatureF property is serialized; Summary is string? and may be null."
